[[:db/retract 17592186160832 :answer-field/choices 17592186160833] [:db/retract 17592186160832 :answer-field/choices 17592186160834] [:db/retract 17592186160832 :answer-field/choices 17592186160835] [:db/retract 17592186160832 :answer-field/choices 17592186160836] [:db/retract 17592186160832 :answer-field/choices 17592186160837] {:db/id 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6cffcafb-88aa-554a-9e0e-d0b676da85d1" "question-d2074d50-adbe-5509-b588-3fcd898ef1ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161772 :question/problem "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](images/af/af5a3add30b403955409fc5c9315f2607a432461e85e4b129e37e0f8e55245a9.svg)  Evaluate the function when ![](images/ae/aee097401481134f5802be4cba03f62ff46cf5fd0f4860fc85e7a85596d3ae09.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Substituting ![](images/8d/8d6326ecf66d2e20be5893c256b05f45cf986f00aa332e5b2e343a79096af202.svg) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8fd187ae-a269-5381-90d7-f0ba2d5b4ded" "question-bc56657a-b79e-53ee-87cf-34f486cb39d6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161773 :question/problem "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when ![](images/e3/e355ba8664f980f8e06bcbda40adf063d376478e745b9b6b036331a895192c54.svg) and ![](images/7f/7fe125bd6366adb85e10ab5719049e1e0db7c719b4a714f9155efee77a8f604b.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](images/14/14418dfa570c1be7015799f009ad93388a6dd6d04bed48972bc8163351bbeb87.svg) and ![](images/8b/8bc4748c7c554dc1edfbdce567f9e6d994ebe0955346bfa34712e20286aaa3b3.svg) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161982 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b15d4431-e43f-5101-96e7-ab09f0076b4a" "question-8f253585-3e9e-576c-84e8-68a00302ab3a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161774 :question/problem "![](images/75/7505a6fdbe31e7e3e35e1b9b393d04753b0ccd534e5bacda199e8fc902a5fe3c.svg)\nConsider the matrix ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](images/50/50fa4bc1260a734d8f2a1c3045c81dd58e5148d81b6bd85e901c492ab4f61ead.svg) in terms of the components of ![](images/2c/2c28ae197ea4a26ad524d5e6cc89a18a21bf6f215b14432d5377fb3c8a287b6f.svg) and ![](images/35/356a4d35d556458edf899d2b0a49d6db2d47743c0d029c58e1bd3a3b88d9b8c9.svg)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](images/b6/b6e5dec69a4614a003b3e1e77d18dfb6747cf556fa6f1374803ab0ffc765a3cb.svg) of ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) corresponds to the term ![](images/6e/6e2dccb072d3420de2a0d2d4c9ad9b3f3ff44f62a59c0b3580ced4cdc42f9c9e.svg) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](images/c3/c3b74ef5a2e970298bd4117c499d18a7bc3319c5e4d4c05b83e0e25fb18fba30.svg)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](images/aa/aa4630ec70bc3741e32a93d26aa15090e187b8e660ce611bc80e20e2bd8114e8.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161983 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a33de8e7-0315-5081-b30e-a76239172d51" "question-41f16b5c-e680-54f8-926b-ebe6345d8561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161775 :question/worked-solution "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](images/44/443b1cf1d4425f83b834101627dd202732cf2c905848c8ddbb93dd518f3b35db.svg)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-6cffcafb-88aa-554a-9e0e-d0b676da85d1" :question/id #uuid "6cffcafb-88aa-554a-9e0e-d0b676da85d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-93906" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10-8-3+4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25010ff5-ab1c-5a8c-a044-e8048ed684a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25010ff5-ab1c-5a8c-a044-e8048ed684a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "25010ff5-ab1c-5a8c-a044-e8048ed684a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-276907f5-ae34-5479-a1e4-a7f16d57caea" "answer-fe2ff817-5b1d-5fce-bb2e-2c85c38b3269" "answer-1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" "answer-b6d0a514-3a53-5e57-ba88-4694b5408ef1" "answer-6146082e-e480-5b7d-b409-a06184533a60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-276907f5-ae34-5479-a1e4-a7f16d57caea" :answer/id #uuid "276907f5-ae34-5479-a1e4-a7f16d57caea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe2ff817-5b1d-5fce-bb2e-2c85c38b3269" :answer/id #uuid "fe2ff817-5b1d-5fce-bb2e-2c85c38b3269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" :answer/id #uuid "1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6d0a514-3a53-5e57-ba88-4694b5408ef1" :answer/id #uuid "b6d0a514-3a53-5e57-ba88-4694b5408ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6146082e-e480-5b7d-b409-a06184533a60" :answer/id #uuid "6146082e-e480-5b7d-b409-a06184533a60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d2074d50-adbe-5509-b588-3fcd898ef1ff" :question/id #uuid "d2074d50-adbe-5509-b588-3fcd898ef1ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-93972" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 5+4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =4+15-12 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e18439f9-3a62-5bbd-b03d-810c0b754554"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e18439f9-3a62-5bbd-b03d-810c0b754554" :answer-field/id #uuid "e18439f9-3a62-5bbd-b03d-810c0b754554" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a616642f-842c-5b33-9f13-5521350cd656" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2cde0db6-0613-5460-949f-eec249faca4a" "answer-5cf3348c-7007-546d-af8d-511a3c29d678" "answer-a616642f-842c-5b33-9f13-5521350cd656" "answer-6fefea64-9455-5b69-8388-8876d583feb6" "answer-6fb3e496-52aa-5e82-a11b-96ca9606f2b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cde0db6-0613-5460-949f-eec249faca4a" :answer/id #uuid "2cde0db6-0613-5460-949f-eec249faca4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cf3348c-7007-546d-af8d-511a3c29d678" :answer/id #uuid "5cf3348c-7007-546d-af8d-511a3c29d678" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a616642f-842c-5b33-9f13-5521350cd656" :answer/id #uuid "a616642f-842c-5b33-9f13-5521350cd656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fefea64-9455-5b69-8388-8876d583feb6" :answer/id #uuid "6fefea64-9455-5b69-8388-8876d583feb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fb3e496-52aa-5e82-a11b-96ca9606f2b6" :answer/id #uuid "6fb3e496-52aa-5e82-a11b-96ca9606f2b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8fd187ae-a269-5381-90d7-f0ba2d5b4ded" :question/id #uuid "8fd187ae-a269-5381-90d7-f0ba2d5b4ded" :question/math-academy-id "q-93979" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1fd5e82-7e1e-5e80-89d9-fc63ac2ef995"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1fd5e82-7e1e-5e80-89d9-fc63ac2ef995" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1fd5e82-7e1e-5e80-89d9-fc63ac2ef995" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afe1c099-4476-5cd6-8168-bb6f44c3c646" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2701e16-efe4-5b21-b6fa-6619278a33a6" "answer-afe1c099-4476-5cd6-8168-bb6f44c3c646" "answer-eccf2580-037b-52f5-a74d-d1ddb3539839" "answer-2cff8026-19f3-5d12-8d4a-fdebbba7f5dc" "answer-7b78cc5b-5be7-561b-961d-acbfeed38058"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2701e16-efe4-5b21-b6fa-6619278a33a6" :answer/id #uuid "c2701e16-efe4-5b21-b6fa-6619278a33a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afe1c099-4476-5cd6-8168-bb6f44c3c646" :answer/id #uuid "afe1c099-4476-5cd6-8168-bb6f44c3c646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eccf2580-037b-52f5-a74d-d1ddb3539839" :answer/id #uuid "eccf2580-037b-52f5-a74d-d1ddb3539839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cff8026-19f3-5d12-8d4a-fdebbba7f5dc" :answer/id #uuid "2cff8026-19f3-5d12-8d4a-fdebbba7f5dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b78cc5b-5be7-561b-961d-acbfeed38058" :answer/id #uuid "7b78cc5b-5be7-561b-961d-acbfeed38058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bc56657a-b79e-53ee-87cf-34f486cb39d6" :question/id #uuid "bc56657a-b79e-53ee-87cf-34f486cb39d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93920" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}. \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-0+0-1-2 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4bb5e8f5-c9f7-536e-9428-9ca34ec2e366"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4bb5e8f5-c9f7-536e-9428-9ca34ec2e366" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bb5e8f5-c9f7-536e-9428-9ca34ec2e366" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" "answer-4c939ced-410b-538a-b95e-7eabbbc8766a" "answer-21bd4957-61ca-515f-955c-429ec430a2c2" "answer-66b821eb-cfc5-5167-9c91-37e6e80d6d3f" "answer-56aa150d-8b20-5d1a-b78e-808ac608f56f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" :answer/id #uuid "16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c939ced-410b-538a-b95e-7eabbbc8766a" :answer/id #uuid "4c939ced-410b-538a-b95e-7eabbbc8766a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21bd4957-61ca-515f-955c-429ec430a2c2" :answer/id #uuid "21bd4957-61ca-515f-955c-429ec430a2c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66b821eb-cfc5-5167-9c91-37e6e80d6d3f" :answer/id #uuid "66b821eb-cfc5-5167-9c91-37e6e80d6d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56aa150d-8b20-5d1a-b78e-808ac608f56f" :answer/id #uuid "56aa150d-8b20-5d1a-b78e-808ac608f56f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b15d4431-e43f-5101-96e7-ab09f0076b4a" :question/id #uuid "b15d4431-e43f-5101-96e7-ab09f0076b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93991" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43d9d476-deb7-5159-945c-bd382763aea3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43d9d476-deb7-5159-945c-bd382763aea3" :answer-field/id #uuid "43d9d476-deb7-5159-945c-bd382763aea3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2f621b4-1a27-59a6-9d95-b8cc81fcaf7c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-22b8fa47-b5d7-5475-809f-5b86289a33ef" "answer-f2d475eb-ebf0-5365-a6f5-fdf8e2a293d0" "answer-0b02a7dc-3d77-54f9-9eab-4104398fd87b" "answer-296cb029-fd72-54e6-8b59-ce6e9308ae5f" "answer-a2f621b4-1a27-59a6-9d95-b8cc81fcaf7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22b8fa47-b5d7-5475-809f-5b86289a33ef" :answer/id #uuid "22b8fa47-b5d7-5475-809f-5b86289a33ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2d475eb-ebf0-5365-a6f5-fdf8e2a293d0" :answer/id #uuid "f2d475eb-ebf0-5365-a6f5-fdf8e2a293d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b02a7dc-3d77-54f9-9eab-4104398fd87b" :answer/id #uuid "0b02a7dc-3d77-54f9-9eab-4104398fd87b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-296cb029-fd72-54e6-8b59-ce6e9308ae5f" :answer/id #uuid "296cb029-fd72-54e6-8b59-ce6e9308ae5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2f621b4-1a27-59a6-9d95-b8cc81fcaf7c" :answer/id #uuid "a2f621b4-1a27-59a6-9d95-b8cc81fcaf7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162590 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186160832 :answer-field/correct "answer-989ea25f-37be-568e-b80b-e6e58c5da663" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb109607-0a7d-5ec5-83c6-08f21eea7ccc" "answer-989ea25f-37be-568e-b80b-e6e58c5da663" "answer-46905384-ce8a-5ab9-af0b-2976fe3be6b4" "answer-aaeac9ef-7f69-5e21-b596-8a8eced51973" "answer-08e5bf9a-2ab7-5739-b14d-f546e211c130"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb109607-0a7d-5ec5-83c6-08f21eea7ccc" :answer/id #uuid "eb109607-0a7d-5ec5-83c6-08f21eea7ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-989ea25f-37be-568e-b80b-e6e58c5da663" :answer/id #uuid "989ea25f-37be-568e-b80b-e6e58c5da663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46905384-ce8a-5ab9-af0b-2976fe3be6b4" :answer/id #uuid "46905384-ce8a-5ab9-af0b-2976fe3be6b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaeac9ef-7f69-5e21-b596-8a8eced51973" :answer/id #uuid "aaeac9ef-7f69-5e21-b596-8a8eced51973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08e5bf9a-2ab7-5739-b14d-f546e211c130" :answer/id #uuid "08e5bf9a-2ab7-5739-b14d-f546e211c130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8f253585-3e9e-576c-84e8-68a00302ab3a" :question/id #uuid "8f253585-3e9e-576c-84e8-68a00302ab3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93997" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-5){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-5{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-498a26f3-93fc-5768-8c25-7e9199e29e91"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-498a26f3-93fc-5768-8c25-7e9199e29e91" :answer-field/id #uuid "498a26f3-93fc-5768-8c25-7e9199e29e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8faa3ec-9091-532c-92df-30bbd8e9a9f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8faa3ec-9091-532c-92df-30bbd8e9a9f8" "answer-e1f20766-50fb-5c84-b3d7-0dee5a60c22e" "answer-2c39145d-687d-5e9d-a4b7-4803af6f1033" "answer-6a490a4b-b443-5931-846e-82347d39a8a5" "answer-c19d0695-6a4b-5a8d-8f46-59949e70c5cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8faa3ec-9091-532c-92df-30bbd8e9a9f8" :answer/id #uuid "f8faa3ec-9091-532c-92df-30bbd8e9a9f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1f20766-50fb-5c84-b3d7-0dee5a60c22e" :answer/id #uuid "e1f20766-50fb-5c84-b3d7-0dee5a60c22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c39145d-687d-5e9d-a4b7-4803af6f1033" :answer/id #uuid "2c39145d-687d-5e9d-a4b7-4803af6f1033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a490a4b-b443-5931-846e-82347d39a8a5" :answer/id #uuid "6a490a4b-b443-5931-846e-82347d39a8a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c19d0695-6a4b-5a8d-8f46-59949e70c5cb" :answer/id #uuid "c19d0695-6a4b-5a8d-8f46-59949e70c5cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a33de8e7-0315-5081-b30e-a76239172d51" :question/id #uuid "a33de8e7-0315-5081-b30e-a76239172d51" :question/math-academy-id "q-140864" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & b & -2 \\\\ c & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b-c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b-c=3+(-5)-(-2)=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f518492-fe4d-57a1-9b58-5b5c3a48afb9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f518492-fe4d-57a1-9b58-5b5c3a48afb9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f518492-fe4d-57a1-9b58-5b5c3a48afb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8ef974e9-9b7e-5867-a2a8-3b0562672573" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4a888cc-2671-524d-89a1-f86fe165eae6" "answer-8ef974e9-9b7e-5867-a2a8-3b0562672573" "answer-37fbf637-f056-50e2-b26c-d48cd839d327" "answer-bf99ec69-37cc-5e99-a769-8cf0e13875fb" "answer-43f4a623-1435-5ed2-ab63-86eb0d268aad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4a888cc-2671-524d-89a1-f86fe165eae6" :answer/id #uuid "e4a888cc-2671-524d-89a1-f86fe165eae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ef974e9-9b7e-5867-a2a8-3b0562672573" :answer/id #uuid "8ef974e9-9b7e-5867-a2a8-3b0562672573" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37fbf637-f056-50e2-b26c-d48cd839d327" :answer/id #uuid "37fbf637-f056-50e2-b26c-d48cd839d327" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf99ec69-37cc-5e99-a769-8cf0e13875fb" :answer/id #uuid "bf99ec69-37cc-5e99-a769-8cf0e13875fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43f4a623-1435-5ed2-ab63-86eb0d268aad" :answer/id #uuid "43f4a623-1435-5ed2-ab63-86eb0d268aad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41f16b5c-e680-54f8-926b-ebe6345d8561" :question/id #uuid "41f16b5c-e680-54f8-926b-ebe6345d8561" :question/math-academy-id "q-94050" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+1=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6070624a-322a-55b2-9acf-4b66d4684f47"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6070624a-322a-55b2-9acf-4b66d4684f47" :answer-field/id #uuid "6070624a-322a-55b2-9acf-4b66d4684f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09004ef9-4917-58d2-8c07-5742c23a3707" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff6634ff-8df0-570a-b775-f5f7b0dd5975" "answer-51df2d1f-f33d-542f-95ae-1b7bae1bef78" "answer-09004ef9-4917-58d2-8c07-5742c23a3707" "answer-ab7bf224-6bd2-51db-a931-dd164fe74c50" "answer-4b827265-5f1b-5d21-bc00-5ef126ec2974"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff6634ff-8df0-570a-b775-f5f7b0dd5975" :answer/id #uuid "ff6634ff-8df0-570a-b775-f5f7b0dd5975" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51df2d1f-f33d-542f-95ae-1b7bae1bef78" :answer/id #uuid "51df2d1f-f33d-542f-95ae-1b7bae1bef78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09004ef9-4917-58d2-8c07-5742c23a3707" :answer/id #uuid "09004ef9-4917-58d2-8c07-5742c23a3707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab7bf224-6bd2-51db-a931-dd164fe74c50" :answer/id #uuid "ab7bf224-6bd2-51db-a931-dd164fe74c50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b827265-5f1b-5d21-bc00-5ef126ec2974" :answer/id #uuid "4b827265-5f1b-5d21-bc00-5ef126ec2974" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163225 :tutorial/content "Let $n$ be a positive integer. A  function \n\n$$\nf: \\Bbb R^n \\to \\Bbb R\n$$\n\nis a **linear form**  (or  *linear functional*) if there is a row-vector \n\n![](images/95/952d8832a903cf184286698e449da84d94d61cb46d984a48f33f406a42a8007a.svg)\n\nsuch that for any ![](images/6b/6b756f37311a5e7f4e6cfb160a37b31d54b2ce1e29849044101dc82d49e44d21.svg) we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={a}_{1}{x}_{1}+{a}_{2}{x}_{2}+…+{a}_{n}{x}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let $f(\\mathbf{x})$ be the linear form   defined on $\\Bbb R^2$ by $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](images/26/26cf6eb0836041b648c29908c8d13ae132e644ea68c772e81e011470283c3427.svg) \n\nSuppose we want to evaluate $f(\\mathbf{x})$ at ![](images/5d/5d6ebda5e8563d23b66cdf15f4a47a1ae712510eeacbe6bcebd031534bcc841a.svg) Then, we simply substitute ![](images/6c/6c79170289a47e3ebb2a7226432938640c63ccea0d032e674d4f03967c12c8ea.svg) and obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163234 :tutorial/content "Let $n$ be a positive integer. A  function $B: \\Bbb R^n\\times \\Bbb R^n \\to \\Bbb R$ is said to be a **bilinear form** if there is an $n\\times n$   matrix $A$ such that \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}) =  \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A\\mathbf{y}, \\qquad  \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\in \\Bbb R^n.\n$$\n\nSuppose, for example, that ![](images/e3/e3ef7815e373c266abf34e4bbba1dd9b29adf2865721afeb8bf4e3eb44b105dc.svg) To  evaluate the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{y}$ when ![](images/ac/ac7f10624ad2b9d0807018976526311423dc4110a98ba24f4ff7eac6760af616.svg) and ![](images/5a/5a074c9193bbe395506549cb69b1b2e84d1208211efb1008a5192989850606ce.svg) we substitute  these vectors in the above expression as follows \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo write down our bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ above in terms of vector components \n\n![](images/c4/c47fc6c2d7df7ced599a643531bc19656c7c62915930583089df641e493680e5.svg)\n\nwe proceed as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162217 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
